From e2311add232c7ca0f80951d1a34703ffca16519a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TrinityXSX <trinityxsx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:08:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TrinityXSX: tests for the Touchpad menu pause, Vulkan hooks,
 root argument replay and VKD3D feature level

Unit tests for the XCL-side changes of patches 0020, 0022, 0023 and
0026, each in a trinityxsx_tests module at the end of the file so they
stay out of the way of upstream's own tests on rebase:

- present.rs: title_menu_open() is false (and stays false) on stock
  Windows, where ntdll rejects the PS5 runner's info class; the
  PwTitleMenuSnapshot layout matches the runner's C struct
  pw_title_menu (offsets, 836 bytes); wrap_vulkan_proc and the
  vkGetInstanceProcAddr / vkGetDeviceProcAddr / vkQueuePresentKHR
  hooks forward to fake loader entry points and fail safe before they
  are resolved.
- bind.rs: PC graphics root arguments are recorded per index and kind,
  constants in call order, cleared on signature change / ClearState /
  Reset, copied to split lists, and replayed after the root signature
  on a PC-pipeline draw.
- console_heap.rs: pc_gpu_handle for views, samplers, CPU-only heaps,
  32-bit console addresses and the shared heap.
- config.rs: vkd3d_feature_level defaults to empty, is read from
  xcl.toml and is optional.
